From dc861cc5a4980aecef4aa59b09070150cdb88848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 01:12:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 3-point as mupen64plus/GLideN64; SwitchDisc hotkey; hide
 cursor in fullscreen; launcher ui_scale plumbing

3-Point (N64) is now the float formulation mupen64plus renders through
GLideN64 (glsl_CombinerProgramBuilderAccurate.cpp, ArthurCarvalho /
twinaphex for mupen64plus-libretro): c0 = c00 + s(c10-c00) + t(c01-c00),
c1 = c11 + (1-s)(c01-c11) + (1-t)(c10-c11), c0 + step(1, s+t)(c1-c0),
with premultiplied-alpha colour bleeding handling; the RDP integer
datapath is gone. [KeyMap] SwitchDisc restarts into the next installed
sibling disc (the launcher's Switch button as a hotkey). [video]
hide_cursor_fullscreen (default on) hides the pointer while fullscreen,
polled per frame so every entry path counts; the F1 menu shows it.
[launcher] ui_scale (75..200 %) carried for the launcher's scale slider.
